## Implementation order

**Step 1 — Domain entities** (`Forgia.Domain`)
- `Printer` — name, power_w (int), purchase_cost (decimal), useful_life_h (decimal), maintenance_€_per_h (decimal)
- `FilamentSpool` — name, material, cost_per_kg (decimal), current stock
- `Customer` — name, contact
- `Order` — customer ref, created date, margin_rate, vat_rate
- `Project` — order ref, name
- `Plate` — project ref, printer ref, spool ref, print_time (TimeSpan), filament_usage_g (decimal), waste_rate
- `LaborActivity` — order ref, description, minutes (decimal), hourly_rate (decimal)
- `QuoteCalculator` — full formula per CLAUDE.md, canonical in `Domain/Pricing/`

**Step 2 — Unit tests** (`Forgia.Domain.Tests`)
- All formula branches on `QuoteCalculator` (mandatory per GUIDELINES)

**Step 3 — Infrastructure** (`Forgia.Infrastructure`)
- EF Core mappings for all entities (no generic repos)
- `ForgiaDbContext` populated with DbSets
- New EF migration

**Step 4 — File parsers** (`Forgia.Infrastructure`)
- 3MF parser → extracts print time + filament usage from `.3mf` metadata
- G-code parser → extracts same from slicer comments (`;` lines)

**Step 5 — PDF export** (`Forgia.Infrastructure`)
- QuestPDF document: customer, order lines, cost breakdown, total

**Step 6 — UI wizard** (`Forgia.UI`)
- File drop (drag + browse) → auto-detect 3MF/G-code
- Printer + filament spool pickers (seeded from DB)
- Cost breakdown display (live-calculated)
- Export PDF button
- `Strings.resx` for all user-facing strings

**Step 7 — Seed data** (dev only, not shipping)
- One example printer + spool so wizard works on first launch

**Step 8 — Migration + MEMORY.md entry + commits**

